{
  "dom_id": "step-q23396",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "If $m∠A=(5x+16)^{∘}$ and $m∠B=(x+8)^{∘},$ find a value of $x$ that satisfies $\\operatorname{cot}⁡A=\\operatorname{tan}⁡B.$  Suppose that both $∠A$ and $∠B$ are acute.",
  "worked_solution": "If both angles are acute and $\\operatorname{cot}⁡A=\\operatorname{tan}⁡B,$ then the angles $∠A$ and $∠B$ must be complementary, and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x+16)^{∘}+(x+8)^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ (6x+24)^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 6x+24 & =90 \\\\ 6x & =66 \\\\ x & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
